# Exercises every Reviews & Ratings endpoint against the compose stack (`make up`). The reads need
# no token. Writing a review needs a Customer who has paid for the Product: check out a Google
# Pixel 9 as demo@ecomm.local on the Storefront first, or the post below is a 403 `notPurchased`.
# Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the token requests store tokens for
# the ones after them, and the post stores the review's ID. Staff moderate as the seeded
# staff@ecomm.local. Reporting the demo Customer's review needs a second Customer: register one on
# the Storefront first, and put its email and password in @otherEmail and @otherPassword below.

@reviews = http://localhost:8097
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@otherEmail = other@ecomm.local
@otherPassword = change-me

### A Product's reviews, newest first: page from 0, 10 to a page unless `size` says (up to 50)
GET {{reviews}}/products/PHN-PIXEL-9/reviews?page=0&size=10

### A Product's rating summary: the average to one decimal (null without reviews), the count, and the count per star
GET {{reviews}}/products/PHN-PIXEL-9/rating-summary

### Many Products' summaries at once, in the order asked: up to 50 SKUs
GET {{reviews}}/rating-summaries?sku=PHN-PIXEL-9&sku=PHN-IPHONE-16&sku=LPT-MBA-13-M3

### More than 50 SKUs, or none: 400
GET {{reviews}}/rating-summaries

### Customer token. The scope brings the given and family names a review's display name is made from.
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo&scope=openid profile

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### May I review it? `eligible`, or a `reason`: notPurchased or alreadyReviewed, with my review
GET {{reviews}}/products/PHN-PIXEL-9/eligibility
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Post a review: 201, or 403 notPurchased, or 409 alreadyReviewed. The title is optional.
POST {{reviews}}/products/PHN-PIXEL-9/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rating": 4, "title": "Great camera", "body": "Sharp photos, and the battery lasts a day."}

> {% client.global.set("reviewId", response.body.id); %}

### A screened word, posted or edited, holds a review: HELD, not listed or counted until Staff publish it; its author sees its status in the eligibility answer, and an edit that clears the screen publishes it
PUT {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rating": 4, "title": "Not a scam", "body": "Sharp photos, and the battery lasts a day."}

### An invalid review: a rating outside 1 to 5, a title over 120 characters or a blank body is a 400
POST {{reviews}}/products/PHN-PIXEL-9/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rating": 6, "body": " "}

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The moderation queue: held reviews and published ones with open reports, oldest first, with openReports by reason
GET {{reviews}}/moderation/reviews?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Publish the held review: it is listed and counted; 409 notHeld once it is published
POST {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The second Customer's token, to report the demo Customer's review
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username={{otherEmail}}&password={{otherPassword}}

> {% client.global.set("otherToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Report it: SPAM, OFFENSIVE, OFF_TOPIC or OTHER, and an optional note. 201; again, 200 with the first report. My own review is a 403 ownReview.
POST {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "OFF_TOPIC", "note": "About the seller, not the phone."}

### Any review as Staff see it: its author's Customer ID, every report and its moderation history
GET {{reviews}}/moderation/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Dismiss a published review's open reports: it stays up and leaves the queue; 409 noOpenReports without any
POST {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/dismiss-reports
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Remove a review with a reason its author sees: 400 without one, 409 alreadyRemoved once removed
POST {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/remove
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Reviews are of the product, not of the seller."}

### Its author sees it REMOVED with its removalReason
GET {{reviews}}/products/PHN-PIXEL-9/eligibility
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Editing a removed review is a 409 reviewRemoved
PUT {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rating": 5, "body": "Even better after the update."}

### Delete my review, whatever its status: 204; then I may write another
DELETE {{reviews}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
